A batch of small, unrelated UI issues collected over time — each too minor to justify its own
GitHub issue, so they're tracked together as one issue (#90) with one shared Spec file. Unlike
the grouped-file convention for a single staged initiative, these steps aren't ordered or
dependent on each other; they're just being scheduled and shipped together.

---

## Step 1: Add description card to Event Home page

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#90

### Summary
The Event Home page shows the event title and tabs but never surfaces the event's own
description anywhere.

### Reported Behavior
No description text appears on the Event Home tab at all.

### Expected Behavior
A card renders directly under the event title/tabs header (`_EventHeader.cshtml`) containing
the event's description. The card should be short (minimal vertical height) and fairly wide,
with small, centered text.

### Root Cause
Not a regression — the feature was never built. `Home.cshtml` only renders `_EventHeader`
(title/emoji/tabs); nothing downstream of it surfaces `Description`.

### Proposed Fix
Add a new card (or a small section within/after `_EventHeader.cshtml`) on the Event Home view
that renders the event's `Description` field, styled per the "short, wide, centered, small text"
requirement.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Event Home page shows a card under the title heading with the event description.
- Card is visually short (low height) and wide, matching the surrounding card style language.
- Description text is centered and rendered at a smaller font size than body copy.

### Out of Scope
- Editing the description from this page (already handled via Settings).
- Behavior when description is empty/null (confirm with developer before implementing —
  hide the card entirely vs. show an empty-state message).

