## Step 2: Organizer dropdown/list don't handle zero organizers

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#90

### Summary
The "Demote to participant" dropdown on the Organizer permissions card always renders even
when there are no organizers to select, and the "Current organizers" list shows nothing when
empty instead of a message.

### Reported Behavior
On the Settings tab's "Organizer permissions" card, "Select an organizer" (the demote dropdown)
is shown even when `Model.Organizers` is empty. The "Current organizers" section below it
renders an empty list with no indication that there are no organizers.

### Expected Behavior
The demote dropdown should behave like the promote dropdown already does when its list is
empty — hide the `<select>`/confirm button and show an equivalent short message instead (e.g.
"There are no organizers to demote."). The "Current organizers" section should show a
"no organizers yet" message when `Model.Organizers` is empty, instead of an empty list.

### Root Cause
`WhenWorksWeb/Views/Events/Settings.cshtml:99-116` (promote dropdown) already has this
empty-state branch: `if (Model.PromotableParticipants.Count > 0) { <select>... } else { <p>Everyone
here is already an organizer.</p> }`. The demote dropdown at `Settings.cshtml:126-139` has no
equivalent check — it unconditionally renders the `<select>` and iterates `Model.Organizers`,
which is simply empty. The "Current organizers" list at `Settings.cshtml:142-148` similarly has
no empty-state branch around its `@foreach`.

### Proposed Fix
Mirror the promote dropdown's existing pattern for the demote dropdown (`Settings.cshtml:126-139`):
wrap it in `if (Model.Organizers.Count > 0)` / `else` with a short empty-state message. Add a
similar `if (Model.Organizers.Count > 0)` / `else` around the "Current organizers" list
(`Settings.cshtml:142-148`) with a "no organizers" message in the `else` branch.

### Acceptance Criteria
- With zero organizers, the demote dropdown is replaced by an empty-state message (exact
  copy TBD, following the existing "Everyone here is already an organizer." tone).
- With zero organizers, "Current organizers" shows a message instead of an empty list.
- With one or more organizers, both sections behave exactly as they do today.

### Out of Scope
- Changing the zero-organizer permission fallback logic itself (`CanManageOrganizersAsync`) —
  this is purely the Settings view's empty-state rendering.

