## Step 3: "New Event" button sized differently in hamburger menu

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#90

### Summary
In the collapsed (mobile) hamburger nav, the "New Event" pill doesn't match the size of the
other stacked nav links.

### Reported Behavior
Below the `sm` breakpoint, once the navbar collapses behind the hamburger toggle, "New Event"
renders at a different size than My Events/Account/etc.

### Expected Behavior
"New Event" should match the height/width/padding of its sibling pills in the collapsed menu.

### Root Cause
Likely candidate (needs visual confirmation before fixing): unlike the other nav items, "New
Event" is a `<button>` wrapped in its own `<form class="d-flex">`
(`WhenWorksWeb/Views/Shared/_LoginPartial.cshtml:19-25`), rather than a bare `<a class="nav-link">`.
The collapsed-menu rule `.navbar-collapse .nav-link { display: block; width: 100%; }`
(`site.css:675-685`) targets the `.nav-link` class directly, which the button does carry, but
the icon+"New Event" label combination is longer than the other plain-text labels — at
full-width in a narrow mobile viewport this may wrap to two lines (or otherwise size
differently) where the shorter single-word labels don't, producing a visibly different pill
height/width.

### Proposed Fix
Confirm the actual visual discrepancy (screenshot/devtools at <576px), then align sizing —
likely constraining/adjusting the label so it doesn't wrap, or explicitly matching padding/
line-height between the button and its sibling `<a>` pills in the collapsed-menu media query.

### Acceptance Criteria
- At mobile widths, the "New Event" pill in the hamburger menu visually matches the height
  and width behavior of the other nav pills.

### Out of Scope
- Desktop navbar sizing (not reported as an issue there).

