## Step 4: My Events card avatars wrap into a column instead of a row

### Status
Fixed.

### GitHub Issue
#90

### Summary
Participant avatar circles on My Events cards stack into one long vertical column for events
with multiple participants, instead of flowing left-to-right and wrapping only when a row
runs out of width.

### Reported Behavior
On My Events cards with several participants, avatars cascade into a single column even when
there's clearly enough horizontal space in the card for multiple avatars per row.

### Expected Behavior
Avatars should flow in a row, wrapping onto additional rows only once a row is actually full.

### Root Cause
`.ww-myevent-avatars` (`site.css:1915-1921`) is `display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap;` with
`max-width: 7rem` and no explicit `flex-shrink`/`min-width` of its own. It sits inside
`.ww-myevent-footer` (`site.css:1908-1910`), itself a `d-flex align-items-center
justify-content-between gap-2` row alongside the delete button and "Enter" button
(`MyEvents/Index.cshtml:88-106`). With no min-width reservation, the avatars container can be
squeezed down by its flex siblings to a width that only fits one ~1.7rem circle per row,
producing the reported single-column cascade instead of true multi-avatar rows. Needs
confirmation via devtools (checking the container's actual computed width when this happens),
but this is the strongest candidate.

### Proposed Fix
Give `.ww-myevent-avatars` a `min-width` (or `flex-shrink: 0` sized to fit a reasonable number
of avatars, e.g. 2-3) so its siblings in `.ww-myevent-footer` don't compress it to single-circle
width before shrinking themselves.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Events with 2+ participants show multiple avatars per row on My Events cards at normal card
  widths, wrapping only when actually out of horizontal room.

### Out of Scope
- Avatar circle size/shape itself (not reported as wrong — only the wrapping behavior).

