## Step 5: Nickname input on Event Sign-In turns white after autofill

### Status
Proposed.

### GitHub Issue
#90

### Summary
The Nickname field on the Event Sign-In page loses its yellow pill styling and turns white
after being autofilled by the browser, and doesn't revert once focus leaves the field.

### Reported Behavior
After browser autofill populates the Nickname field, it turns white; clicking away from the
field doesn't restore the normal yellow background.

### Expected Behavior
The field should keep its normal `.input-pill-yellow` styling in every state, matching how it
looks when filled in manually.

### Root Cause
Needs live-browser confirmation before a fix is written — this may be a known, hard Chromium
autofill limitation rather than a straightforward CSS bug. `SignIn.cshtml:45-48` already uses
`.input-pill-yellow`, and `site.css:832-840` already applies the standard inset
`box-shadow`/`-webkit-text-fill-color` autofill override for that exact class. Since that
override exists and targets `:-webkit-autofill` (all pseudo-states) plus the standards-track
`:autofill`, the reported "still turns white after blur" behavior suggests either: (a) some
other rule with higher specificity/later source order is overriding the fix specifically after
blur, or (b) the field's browser/version combination doesn't match `:-webkit-autofill`
reliably after blur (a known Chromium quirk in some versions), or (c) validation-state styling
(`is-invalid`/similar) is involved. Confirm exact browser/version and whether devtools shows
`:-webkit-autofill` still matching after blur before deciding whether this is fixable.

### Proposed Fix
TBD pending investigation above — may be a small CSS specificity fix, or may need to be
documented as a known browser limitation with no full fix available.

### Acceptance Criteria
- Nickname field either keeps its yellow styling after autofill + blur, or — if confirmed
  unfixable — this is documented as a known limitation rather than left as an open bug.

### Out of Scope
- Autofill behavior on any other input/page not reported here.
